```yaml
id: coding/feature
kind: guide
#-- Phần Work lifecycle: GIỮ tới cutover coding; được đọc hôm nay bởi schema steps cho Work driver loop,
#-- chọn operation và kiểm operation hợp lệ của Assignment. Chỉ bỏ các trường runner trên mỗi step.
steps:
  - { id: discovery, phase: discover, skill: fgos-coding-discovering, operations: [ ...giữ nguyên... ] }  # bỏ units
  - { id: exploring, phase: discover, skill: fgos-coding-exploring,   operations: [ ...giữ nguyên... ] }  # bỏ dependsOn, units, gate
  - { id: planning,  phase: plan,     skill: fgos-coding-planning,    operations: [ ...giữ nguyên... ] }  # bỏ dependsOn, units
  - { id: executing, phase: execute,  skill: fgos-coding-implement,   operations: [ ...giữ nguyên... ] }  # bỏ dependsOn, units
  # hai step chỉ-của-runner 'integrate' và 'approval' bị bỏ: không phase, không skill, không operation, chưa từng chạy
transitions: [ {from: discovery, to: exploring}, {from: discovery, to: planning}, {from: exploring, to: planning}, {from: planning, to: executing} ]
aliases: { decompose: planning }
statusSkills: { retrospective: { skill: fgos-coding-knowledge, taskSpec: compound-learn } }
#-- Phần guide: THÊM cạnh phần lifecycle; chưa reader nào dùng cho tới cutover
milestones:
  - id: request-received
  - id: decisions-locked   # subject: artifact quyết định; chấp nhận: consent gate hoặc verdict discovery 'clear'
  - id: plan-validated     # subject: plan.md; chấp nhận: verdict validate-plan (reviewed) + consent validateApprove
  - id: child-verified     # subject: các đường dẫn đã test của con; chấp nhận: verify-receipt
  - id: integrated         # subject: cây tích hợp; chấp nhận: verify-receipt (subject mới)
  - id: approved           # subject: digest cây tích hợp; chấp nhận: consent người
  - id: merged             # guard nền tảng: approve door + mergedSha; không thuộc sáu primitive
activities:                # mỗi activity gọi tên operation nó sẽ thay lúc cutover
  - { id: judge-ambiguity, operation: discovery/judge-ambiguity, entry: [request-received], produces: [decisions-locked], effects: none }
  - { id: lock-decisions,  operation: exploring/lock-decisions,  entry: [request-received], produces: [decisions-locked], effects: none }
  - { id: shape-plan,      operation: planning/shape-plan,       entry: [decisions-locked], produces: [plan-validated],  effects: none }
  - { id: validate-plan,   operation: planning/validate-plan,    entry: [decisions-locked], produces: [plan-validated],  effects: none, unit: { pattern: reviewed } }
  - { id: implement-item,  operation: executing/implement-item,  entry: [plan-validated],   produces: [child-verified],  effects: writes, unit: { pattern: reviewed } }
  - { id: review-item,     operation: executing/review-item,     entry: [child-verified],   produces: [],                effects: none }   # findings là kết cục
  - { id: fix-verify-red,  operation: executing/fix-verify-red,  entry: [plan-validated],   produces: [child-verified],  effects: writes }
  - { id: integrate,       operation: none,                      entry: [child-verified],   produces: [integrated],      effects: writes, unit: { kind: integrate } }
  # resolve-question, scout-blast-radius, scoped-subtask: cùng dạng, entry theo milestone tương ứng
decisions:
  - { at: request-received, should: judge-ambiguity, reason: "một lượt máy rẻ hơn người; nó phán clear/unclear", mayInstead: [lock-decisions] }
  - { at: decisions-locked, should: [shape-plan, validate-plan], reason: "plan đã validate là khung các con chạy dưới đó", mayInstead: [scout-blast-radius] }
  - { at: plan-validated, should: "implement-item cho mỗi con với writes rời nhau", reason: "pattern reviewed bắt hồi quy trước tích hợp", mayInstead: [fix-verify-red, scoped-subtask] }
  - { at: approved, listedRoutesOnly: true }     # cờ có authority chỉ ở decision point
must:
  - { id: no-writes-outside-unit, guard: write-scope-isolation, note: "guard nền tảng, tham chiếu không chép lại" }
  - { id: child-receipt,          guard: verify-receipt, subject: child-verified }
  - { id: integration-receipt,    guard: verify-receipt, subject: integrated, reason: "test trên cây con không chứng minh gì về cây tích hợp (L9)" }
  - { id: consent-before-merge,   guard: human-consent,  subject: approved,   reason: "duyệt cây A không phải duyệt cây B" }
unenforced:
  - { id: tasteful-architecture, becomes: "receipt verdict của review-item", note: "đánh giá ngữ nghĩa là verdict của người đánh giá" }
frameDefaults: { mutatingDispatches: <đặt lúc duyệt từ plan>, seatLaunchesPerDispatch: <tính từ pattern>, fallbackPerSeat: 2, deviationsBeforeAsk: 2 }
closure: [approved]
```

docs/platform/agent-mailbox/spec.md.sectionText:
## 1. Purpose and scope

A coding agent does not listen. Between two model calls nothing is waiting for a message; the agent sees a message only when its harness puts it into the next model call. The Mailbox component owns exactly one decision: **how a message is placed into the context of the right live agent session at the earliest safe point, with an honest report of when that will happen.**

The text of a message travels in one way only: the recipient reads it from the local record, at a checkpoint (a hook) or when it calls `inbox --claim`. A channel that reaches an idle session carries only a one-line signal (a nudge), never the body. This keeps one framing path and one place that enforces policy.

The first slice serves **interactive sessions in a terminal**, the owner's own sessions first. It is not a protocol for confined or headless workers (section 15.7).

**Who can receive (owner, 2026-10-20).** A recipient is a head that was started independently of a runner Unit: a person's own session, or any launch path that is not a Unit attempt. A sender may be any session of the project, the runner or the `fgos` CLI. A Unit attempt (writer id `att-`) is never a recipient, and a subagent or teammate never is. Whoever starts a recipient head owns the line that lists its trusted senders (section 16 question 16). Steering a Unit attempt is the runner's own decision (section 15.4) and would need its own G0.

In scope for the first slice:

- the message envelope and the states of section 5.2;
- the policies that bound a message (size, chain depth, loops, queue, trust class, wake);
- the verbs `send`, `inbox`, `list`, `status` and the receiver-side hook kind `fgos hook mailbox` (section 4.1);
- one outbound port for waking (`Nudge`) and one for session state (`Presence`);
- adapters for Claude Code, Codex and agy, all receiving mail through the `hook mailbox` kind; the wake-capable channels that need no terminal are the Claude Code session socket (scoped sessions only) and `codex queue`; agy has tier `turn` or `pull` and is not woken when idle;
- a local record on one machine (section 6.4);
- conformance tests an adapter must pass, as opt-in live tests.

Out of scope for the first slice, recorded in section 15 so the interfaces keep room for them:

- acknowledgement (`acked`), `handled`, `reply_by`, expiry with dead letters, approval (`held`);
- delivery between machines and anything pushed to a Git remote;
- the pi and omp adapters;
- the typed nudge for an idle agy session, with everything that exists only to support it: the shared crate `fgos-agent-terminal`, the empty-composer verdict, a focus-neutral `deliver_brief`, the attach allocation record and the terminal-control and agent-protocol dependencies (section 15.8);
- headless workers (`cli-spawn`, no pane and no tty): the first slice serves sessions in a terminal; a headless worker is one Unit run owned by the runner (section 15.7);
- human-addressed groups, the rate limit per machine and the collapse of identical bodies.

Out of scope for good:

- a free-form chat system, threads, channels or broadcast by agents (agents address one session);
- a scheduler, a durable job queue or a daemon (V-011 and `docs/platform/event-store/spec.md` section 3 both exclude them);
- permission decisions: a message never grants, asks for or answers a permission;
- locks or leases on files or work items (a separate decision, section 15.4).
- reaching into the subagents or teammates of a CLI: the mailbox works with the head only (principle, section 15.6);
- a head started by the runner (writer id with `fgos_session_identity::ATTEMPT_PREFIX`, `att-`): it is neither registered nor addressable. Its pane is driven by its run supervisor, and mail entering it between brief and result would change what the Unit run saw. `drain` for such a head prints nothing, `list` omits it and `send` to it is refused as an unknown address. Steering a Unit run is the runner's decision (section 15.4). The prefix test is a function exported by session-identity, not a string comparison in this crate (planned: `is_attempt_writer_id`);
- communication authorization (who may address whom) and the budget of a case or Unit: they belong to the coordination foundation (section 5.3).

